Praveen Kumar Rajendran received the B.E. degree in electrical and electronics engineering from Anna University, India, and the M.S. degree from the Future Vehicle Program, Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology, South Korea. Before pursuing the M.S. degree, he worked as a Software Engineer with SL Corporation. He is currently a Computer Vision/AI Research Engineer with Neubility, focusing on improving robot perception. His research interests include deep learning, 3D computer vision, and autonomous driving.
Luiz Felipe Vecchietti received the B.Sc. degree in electronics and computer engineering and the M.Sc. degree from the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro in 2015 and 2017, respectively, and the Ph.D. degree in green transportation from KAIST in 2021. He is currently a Senior Researcher with the Data Science Group, Institute for Basic Science (IBS), South Korea. His research interests include deep reinforcement learning, graph neural networks, computational biology, applied deep learning, improving exploration and credit assignment in single-agent, and multi-agent reinforcement learning. He has previous research experience in natural language processing, speech synthesis, and robotic applications using continuous control.

Sumit Mishra received the B.Tech. degree in electronics and communication engineering from Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam Technical University, India, in 2016, and the M.S. degree from the Robotics Department, Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology, South Korea, in 2023, where he is currently pursuing the Ph.D. degree. Earlier, he worked with Learnogether Technologies Pvt. Ltd., as a Research Consultant. His research interests include deep learning, computer vision, and robotics perception using multi-modal data.

Dongsoo Har (Senior Member, IEEE) received the B.Sc. and M.Sc. degrees in electronics engineering from Seoul National University and the Ph.D. degree in electrical engineering from Polytechnic University, Brooklyn, NY, USA. He is currently a Faculty Member of KAIST. He has authored and published more than 100 articles in international journals and conferences. He has also presented invited talks and keynote in international conferences. His main research interests include optimization of communication system operation and transportation system development with embedded artificial intelligence. He was a member of the advisory board, the program chair, the vice chair, and the general chair of international conferences. He was a recipient of the Best Paper Award (Jack Neubauer Award) from the IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON VEHICULAR TECHNOLOGY in 2000. He is an Associate Editor of the IEEE SENSORS JOURNAL.

